msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:341
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Step 5. Creating a custom \"status\" schema\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:343
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repo collections are typed, meaning that they have a defined schema. The `app.bsky.actor.profile` type definition [can be found here](https://github.com/bluesky-social/atproto/blob/main/lexicons/app/bsky/actor/profile.json).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:345
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anybody can create a new schema using the [Lexicon](https://atproto.com/specs/lexicon) language, which is very similar to [JSON-Schema](http://json-schema.org/). The schemas use [reverse-DNS IDs](https://atproto.com/specs/nsid) which indicate ownership. In this demo app we're going to use `xyz.statusphere` which we registered specifically for this project (aka statusphere.xyz).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:349
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> ### Why create a schema?\n"
">\n"
"> Schemas help other applications understand the data your app is creating. By publishing your schemas, you make it easier for other application authors to publish data in a format your app will recognize and handle.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:351
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's create our schema in the `/lexicons` folder of our codebase. You can [read more about how to define schemas here](https://atproto.com/guides/lexicon).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:381
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```json\n"
"/** lexicons/status.json **/\n"
"{\n"
"  \"lexicon\": 1,\n"
"  \"id\": \"xyz.statusphere.status\",\n"
"  \"defs\": {\n"
"    \"main\": {\n"
"      \"type\": \"record\",\n"
"      \"key\": \"tid\",\n"
"      \"record\": {\n"
"        \"type\": \"object\",\n"
"        \"required\": [\"status\", \"createdAt\"],\n"
"        \"properties\": {\n"
"          \"status\": {\n"
"            \"type\": \"string\",\n"
"            \"minLength\": 1,\n"
"            \"maxGraphemes\": 1,\n"
"            \"maxLength\": 32\n"
"          },\n"
"          \"createdAt\": {\n"
"            \"type\": \"string\",\n"
"            \"format\": \"datetime\"\n"
"          }\n"
"        }\n"
"      }\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:383
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let's run some code-generation using our schema:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:387
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```bash\n"
"./node_modules/.bin/lex gen-server ./src/lexicon ./lexicons/*\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:389
#, no-wrap
msgid "This will produce TypeScript interfaces as well as runtime validation functions that we can use in our app. Here's what that generated code looks like:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:397
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"/** src/lexicon/types/xyz/statusphere/status.ts **/\n"
"export interface Record {\n"
"  status: string\n"
"  createdAt: string\n"
"  [k: string]: unknown\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:405
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"export function isRecord(v: unknown): v is Record {\n"
"  return (\n"
"    isObj(v) &&\n"
"    hasProp(v, '$type') &&\n"
"    (v.$type === 'xyz.statusphere.status#main' || v.$type === 'xyz.statusphere.status')\n"
"  )\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:410
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"export function validateRecord(v: unknown): ValidationResult {\n"
"  return lexicons.validate('xyz.statusphere.status#main', v)\n"
"}\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:412
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's use that code to improve the `POST /status` route:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:422
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"/** src/routes.ts **/\n"
"import * as Status from '#/lexicon/types/xyz/statusphere/status'\n"
"// ...\n"
"// \"Set status\" handler\n"
"router.post(\n"
"  '/status',\n"
"  handler(async (req, res) => {\n"
"    // ...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:432
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Construct & validate their status record\n"
"    const record = {\n"
"      $type: 'xyz.statusphere.status',\n"
"      status: req.body?.status,\n"
"      createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (!Status.validateRecord(record).success) {\n"
"      return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid status' })\n"
"    }\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:437 src/guides/applications/en.mdx:563
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // ...\n"
"  })\n"
")\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:439
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Step 6. Listening to the firehose\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:441
#, no-wrap
msgid "So far, we have:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:445
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- Logged in via OAuth\n"
"- Created a custom schema\n"
"- Read & written records for the logged in user\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:447
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we want to fetch the status records from other users.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:449
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remember how we referred to our app as being like Google, crawling around the repos to get their records? One advantage we have in the AT Protocol is that each repo publishes an event log of their updates.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:451
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Image alt=\"A diagram of the event stream\" src={DiagramEventStream} />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:453
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using a [Relay service](https://docs.bsky.app/docs/advanced-guides/federation-architecture#relay) we can listen to an aggregated firehose of these events across all users in the network. In our case what we're looking for are valid `xyz.statusphere.status` records.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:459
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"/** src/ingester.ts **/\n"
"import { Firehose } from '@atproto/sync'\n"
"import * as Status from '#/lexicon/types/xyz/statusphere/status'\n"
"// ...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:466
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"new Firehose({\n"
"  filterCollections: ['xyz.statusphere.status'],\n"
"  handleEvent: async (evt) => {\n"
"    // Watch for write events\n"
"    if (evt.event === 'create' || evt.event === 'update') {\n"
"      const record = evt.record\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:480
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      // If the write is a valid status update\n"
"      if (\n"
"        evt.collection === 'xyz.statusphere.status' &&\n"
"        Status.isRecord(record) &&\n"
"        Status.validateRecord(record).success\n"
"      ) {\n"
"        // Store the status\n"
"        // TODO\n"
"      }\n"
"    }\n"
"  },\n"
"})\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:482
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's create a SQLite table to store these statuses:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:495
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"/** src/db.ts **/\n"
"// Create our statuses table\n"
"await db.schema\n"
"  .createTable('status')\n"
"  .addColumn('uri', 'varchar', (col) => col.primaryKey())\n"
"  .addColumn('authorDid', 'varchar', (col) => col.notNull())\n"
"  .addColumn('status', 'varchar', (col) => col.notNull())\n"
"  .addColumn('createdAt', 'varchar', (col) => col.notNull())\n"
"  .addColumn('indexedAt', 'varchar', (col) => col.notNull())\n"
"  .execute()\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:497
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we can write these statuses into our database as they arrive from the firehose:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:525
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"/** src/ingester.ts **/\n"
"// If the write is a valid status update\n"
"if (\n"
"  evt.collection === 'xyz.statusphere.status' &&\n"
"  Status.isRecord(record) &&\n"
"  Status.validateRecord(record).success\n"
") {\n"
"  // Store the status in our SQLite\n"
"  await db\n"
"    .insertInto('status')\n"
"    .values({\n"
"      uri: evt.uri.toString(),\n"
"      authorDid: evt.author,\n"
"      status: record.status,\n"
"      createdAt: record.createdAt,\n"
"      indexedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n"
"    })\n"
"    .onConflict((oc) =>\n"
"      oc.column('uri').doUpdateSet({\n"
"        status: record.status,\n"
"        indexedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n"
"      })\n"
"    )\n"
"    .execute()\n"
"}\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:527
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can almost think of information flowing in a loop:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:529 src/guides/applications/en.mdx:593
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:665
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Image alt=\"A diagram of the flow of information\" src={DiagramInfoFlow} />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:531
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applications write to the repo. The write events are then emitted on the firehose where they're caught by the apps and ingested into their databases.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:533
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why sync from the event log like this? Because there are other apps in the network that will write the records we're interested in. By subscribing to the event log, we ensure that we catch all the data we're interested in &mdash; including data published by other apps!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:535
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Step 7. Listing the latest statuses\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:537
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we have statuses populating our SQLite, we can produce a timeline of status updates by users. We also use a [DID](https://atproto.com/specs/did)-to-handle resolver so we can show a nice username with the statuses:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:545
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"/** src/routes.ts **/\n"
"// Homepage\n"
"router.get(\n"
"  '/',\n"
"  handler(async (req, res) => {\n"
"    // ...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:553
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Fetch data stored in our SQLite\n"
"    const statuses = await db\n"
"      .selectFrom('status')\n"
"      .selectAll()\n"
"      .orderBy('indexedAt', 'desc')\n"
"      .limit(10)\n"
"      .execute()\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:558
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Map user DIDs to their domain-name handles\n"
"    const didHandleMap = await resolver.resolveDidsToHandles(\n"
"      statuses.map((s) => s.authorDid)\n"
"    )\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:565
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our HTML can now list these status records:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:583
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```html\n"
"<!-- src/pages/home.ts -->\n"
"${statuses.map((status, i) => {\n"
"  const handle = didHandleMap[status.authorDid] || status.authorDid\n"
"  return html`\n"
"    <div class=\"status-line\">\n"
"      <div>\n"
"        <div class=\"status\">${status.status}</div>\n"
"      </div>\n"
"      <div class=\"desc\">\n"
"        <a class=\"author\" href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/${handle}\">@${handle}</a>\n"
"        was feeling ${status.status} on ${status.indexedAt}.\n"
"      </div>\n"
"    </div>\n"
"  `\n"
"})}\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:585
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Image alt=\"A screenshot of the app status timeline\" src={AppStatusHistory} />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:587
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Step 8. Optimistic updates\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:589
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a final optimization, let's introduce \"optimistic updates.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:591
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remember the information flow loop with the repo write and the event log?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:595
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since we're updating our users' repos locally, we can short-circuit that flow to our own database:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:597
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Image alt=\"A diagram illustrating optimistic updates\" src={DiagramOptimisticUpdate} />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:599
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is an important optimization to make, because it ensures that the user sees their own changes while using your app. When the event eventually arrives from the firehose, we just discard it since we already have it saved locally.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:601
#, no-wrap
msgid "To do this, we just update `POST /status` to include an additional write to our SQLite DB:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:609
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"/** src/routes.ts **/\n"
"// \"Set status\" handler\n"
"router.post(\n"
"  '/status',\n"
"  handler(async (req, res) => {\n"
"    // ...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:624
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    let uri\n"
"    try {\n"
"      // Write the status record to the user's repository\n"
"      const res = await agent.com.atproto.repo.putRecord({\n"
"        repo: agent.assertDid, \n"
"        collection: 'xyz.statusphere.status',\n"
"        rkey: TID.nextStr(),\n"
"        record,\n"
"      })\n"
"      uri = res.uri\n"
"    } catch (err) {\n"
"      logger.warn({ err }, 'failed to write record')\n"
"      return res.status(500).json({ error: 'Failed to write record' })\n"
"    }\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:643
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    try {\n"
"      // Optimistically update our SQLite <-- HERE!\n"
"      await db\n"
"        .insertInto('status')\n"
"        .values({\n"
"          uri,\n"
"          authorDid: agent.assertDid, \n"
"          status: record.status,\n"
"          createdAt: record.createdAt,\n"
"          indexedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n"
"        })\n"
"        .execute()\n"
"    } catch (err) {\n"
"      logger.warn(\n"
"        { err },\n"
"        'failed to update computed view; ignoring as it should be caught by the firehose'\n"
"      )\n"
"    }\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:650
#, no-wrap
msgid "You'll notice this code looks almost exactly like what we're doing in `ingester.ts`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:652
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Thinking in atproto\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:654
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial we've covered the key steps to building an atproto app. Data is published in its canonical form on users' `at://` repos and then aggregated into apps' databases to produce views of the network.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:656
#, no-wrap
msgid "When building your app, think in these four key steps:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:661
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- Design the [Lexicon](https://atproto.com/guides/lexicon) schemas for the records you'll publish into the Atmosphere.\n"
"- Create a database for aggregating the records into useful views.\n"
"- Build your application to write the records on your users' repos.\n"
"- Listen to the firehose to aggregate data across the network.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:663
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remember this flow of information throughout:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/applications/en.mdx:667
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is how every app in the Atmosphere works, including the [Bluesky social app](https://bsky.app).\n"
msgstr ""

